Command Syntax Description <code>Hostname</code> <code>Hostname</code> Queries the current runtime network hostname. <code>IPAddress</code> <code>IPAddress</code> or <code>IPAddress&lt;1..5&gt;</code> Queries all configured addresses (<code>1</code>: IP, <code>2</code>: Gateway, <code>3</code>: Subnet, <code>4</code>: DNS1, <code>5</code>: DNS2) or one indexed address. <code>WifiScan</code> <code>WifiScan [1]</code> Performs an asynchronous scan and lists detected APs (SSID, RSSI, channel, BSSID, security mode). <code>WifiTest</code> <code>WifiTest &lt;ssid&gt;,&lt;password&gt;</code> Tests station connection to candidate credentials without saving them or dropping existing links. Joins the first access point with that SSID it finds and gives up after 9 s, as Tasmota does (12 s on BL602). <code>DeviceName</code> <code>DeviceName [name]</code> Sets or queries the human-readable device name (up to 31 bytes), distinct from the runtime network hostname. <code>Ping</code> <code>Ping &lt;host&gt;</code> or <code>Ping&lt;0..8&gt; &lt;host&gt;</code> Runs an asynchronous IPv4 ICMP ping campaign. <code>Ping</code> sends 1 probe; <code>Ping1</code>–<code>Ping8</code> send N probes; <code>Ping0</code> makes up to four attempts and stops at the first reply. Querying <code>Ping</code> or <code>Ping ?</code> returns the latest campaign stats. <code>wget</code> <code>wget &lt;URL&gt;</code> Asynchronously downloads direct HTTP 200 file from URL to LittleFS (saving to the URL basename, or <code>/index.html</code>), atomically replacing on success. Querying <code>wget</code> reports progress. <p>Check connection status at any time with <code>Status 5</code> — the <code>IPAddress</code> it reports is where the web UI lives:</p> <pre><code>&gt; Status 5
{"StatusNET":{"Hostname":"newmota-A1B2","IPAddress":"192.168.1.50","Gateway":"192.168.1.1","Subnetmask":"255.255.255.0","DNSServer1":"192.168.1.1","DNSServer2":"0.0.0.0","Mac":"24:4C:AB:12:34:56"}}

&gt; Ping 1.1.1.1
{"Ping":"Done"}

&gt; Ping
{"Ping":{"State":"completed","Destination":"1.1.1.1","Sent":1,"Success":1,"Timeout":0,"Error":""}}

&gt; wget http://192.168.1.100:8000/autoexec.be
{"wget":"Started"}
</code></pre> <p>The connected Wi-Fi band appears as <code>Band</code> (<code>2.4GHz</code> or <code>5GHz</code>) in <code>STATE</code>, <code>Status 5</code> and the web Information page after the first link refresh.</p>
